"And then I added\n\n> It's funny\n> Last time we went back and forth on this\n> I ended up having multiple occasions within the following few days to make similar points in other contexts\n\nMatt’s reply:\n\n> I think you ultimately get to the point that fitting the mold of the MCU style and continuity will destroy the creative freedom of these films and directors will rather work with properties that they have more control over \rThis isn't gonna be a 40 year franchise\n\nAnd mine:\n\n> That's very true\n> That may also be a factor that accelerates the end of the MCU\n\nMatt:\n\n> Let's be honest, can you say you like any of the directors aside from Raimi and Coogler?\rI like Reeves and Gunn\rI'm not particularly attached to any creative at Marvel outside of Korey\rSo I'll be done with it personally once he leaves\\. \rI might be done with it post Secret War given the current quality of things\n\nMe:\n\n> Less and less as time goes on and they get more and more names who don't stand out\\.\rI'm too excited for Fantastic Four and X\\-Men to leave after Secret Wars, but his departure will definitely make me\\.\\.\\.\\. well, I'll be scrutinizing a lot more to see what changes\\."
